. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
.         
.         
.         *The model examines the effect of having at least one daughter (has_d
> aughter) on political ideology (left), testing whether this effect differs by
>  gender through an interaction term between sex and has_daughter. It controls
>  for the total number of children (nb_kid), age (age) and age squared (age2),
>  as well as socio-economic variables (plh0182, hghinc), and includes fixed ef
> fects for family standard (pgfamstd), bilateral relations (pgpsbil), employme
> nt status (pgemplst), survey year (syear), sample region (sampreg), migration
>  background (migback), and gender (sex). The significance and sign of the int
> eraction term i.sex#i.has_daughter indicate whether having daughters impacts 
> men and women differently, thus testing hypothesis H4 that this effect is str
> onger for men.
.         
.         *As an example, and for illustrative purposes we consider a linear OL
> S regression
.         
.         
.          reg left 1.sex#i.has_daughter nb_kid age age2  plh0182 hghinc i.(pgf
> amstd pgpsbil pgemplst syear sampreg migback)  if age>15, cluster(pid) robu

